SCORE: TRANSITION_GEODESIC_FINE_MARGIN | behavior_evidence=4 | geometry_necessity=3 | novelty=UNKNOWN | downstream_mechanism=4 | falsifiability=4 | implementability=3 | exploration_value=3
SCOPE: TRANSITION_GEODESIC_FINE_MARGIN | IN_SCOPE | Directed training transitions and Poincare log/exp plus geodesic prediction error jointly scale fine assignment logits and train the map; behavior-off, Euclidean geometry-off, and both-on are specified. One run only is compatible with policy.
EVIDENCE: TRANSITION_GEODESIC_FINE_MARGIN | E1 E2 E3 E5 E10 E11 E12 E13 E14 E15 E16
OBJECTION: TRANSITION_GEODESIC_FINE_MARGIN | Multiplying every code distance for a given item by the same positive factor preserves its hard argmin; the proposed behavior-to-logit path may therefore alter soft gradients but not exported hard SIDs directly, and could be neutralized by temperature/gradient scaling.
COUNTEREXAMPLE: TRANSITION_GEODESIC_FINE_MARGIN | For distances (1,4) and any positive multiplier (1+e/s), the argmin remains code 1; hence hard assignments do not change from this scaling alone.
RATIONALE: TRANSITION_GEODESIC_FINE_MARGIN | Behavior=4 from measured entropy stratification and coverage (E5,E10). Geometry=3: a real curved prediction path, but no case that matched Euclidean prediction cannot reproduce (E11-E14). Novelty=UNKNOWN because prior work is NOT_CHECKED (E15); bounded check: targeted prior-art and ledger comparison. Downstream=4 because error modifies fine soft logits and trains map/residuals, though hard assignment invariance is a risk. Falsifiability=4: the three switches and prediction/assignment diagnostics are specified. Implementability=3: equations and sparse-edge cost are given, but numerical safeguards and details for invalid ball inputs are incomplete. Exploration=3; an informative residual-level failure is possible. No Recall prediction is inferred.

